  "title": "daemon dispatch: a render error on the main execute path must hold the task visibly (R22 gap)",
  "spec": "Observed 2026-09-22 14:12Z on T-0773: its spec quoted literal double-brace placeholders, so spawn.render(\"execute\", ...) raised ValueError unfilled_placeholder inside daemon.dispatch's main loop (daemon.py ~853-856: `packet = spawn.packet(...)`, `prompt = spawn.render(\"execute\", ...)`, `spawn_async(_dispatch_worker, ...)`, `complete(t[\"id\"], \"dispatched_at\")`). The exception escaped the per-task block: dispatched_at stayed stamped, no event, no hold, the task sat \"queued\" and was silently re-attempted every lease (three memory-recall rows, no execute rows). R22 (T-0755/T-0757) added render-error holds for _dispatch_fresh_fix and spawn.run_worker but not this path.\nDo: wrap the packet build + render + spawn_async of the main execute dispatch path in try/except; on exception call hold_failed(t[\"id\"], \"dispatch_error\", \"dispatch\", e) (existing helper at daemon.py ~484) so the task is held with hold_reason \"dispatch failed: ValueError\" and pipeline.dispatch_error carries the message, never leaving dispatched_at stamped on a task that did not launch (clear it in the same locked update). Also make _dispatch_worker (daemon.py ~496-535) handle every executor.start status: \"held\"/\"budget\" \u2192 clear dispatched_at and set status queued with pipeline.hold_note (held) so the next tick retries; \"refused\"/\"incompatible\" \u2192 post_result failed with the reason; \"fallback\" \u2192 leave as is (the Claude worker owns the task). Today only done/failed are handled and any other status leaves the task queued with dispatched_at stamped.\nTests (unittest): tests/test_daemon.py::test_dispatch_render_error_holds_task (an execute task whose spec contains a literal double-brace token: after one tick the task is held with hold_reason starting \"dispatch failed\" and pipeline.dispatch_error mentions unfilled_placeholder; dispatched_at is not set), tests/test_daemon.py::test_dispatch_worker_handles_non_terminal_start_statuses (executor.start patched to return {\"status\": \"held\", ...} then {\"status\": \"refused\", \"reason\": \"x\"}: first leaves the task queued without dispatched_at and with a hold_note, second posts a failed result with the reason). Keep all existing daemon tests green.",
